      "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lammps/lammps/tarball/patch_13Nov2026",
      "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/lammps/lammps/zipball/patch_13Nov2026",
      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nThis feature release consist mostly of changes that were deferred from the 30 September stable release because they were not ready for merging before we started the extended stable testing phase.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\nThis release includes the following changes:\r\n- add pair style mesomem/dipole, a solvent-free, one-particle-thick coarse-grained membrane model that utilizes each particle's dipole vector direction. (Pietro Sillano, TU Delft) PR #5193\r\n- add an extended-Lagrangian charge equilibration to the QEQ package as new fix styles qeq/point/xlmd, qeq/shielded/xlmd, and qeq/slater/xlmd including REAXFF, OPENMP and KOKKOS variants (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5079 and PR #5242\r\n- add a `fix symmetry` command (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #4997 \r\n- modernize/recreate several Howto tutorials, especially the WSL and the GitHub tutorials, to reflect the current state and use consistent command line conventions throughout the manual plus other minor related corrections (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5226\r\n- apply more best practices for software security and release processing (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5229\r\n- final step in the refactor the management of lists of computes and fixes in the Modify class and removal old APIs (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5267 \r\n- change FFmpeg and gzip detection from a compile-time check to a run time check and use the detected full path when launching it to convert images to movies (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5221\r\n- modernize and improve CUDA and HIP support for the GPU package. remove outdated device sorting. (Trung Nguyen, U Chicago, Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5198 \r\n- add more pair styles to the KOKKOS and OPENMP package (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5246 \r\n- add more pair styles to the GPU package (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5247\r\n- add OPENMP package version of pair style pace (Lorenzo Piersante, EPFL) PR #5243 \r\n- add  `compute mbar` to the FEP package implementing the MBAR method (Agilio Padua, ENS de Lyon) PR #5034\r\n- add new contact models and reorganize granular pair style documentation (Dan Bolintineau, SNL) PR #5219\r\n- add support for more styles in the OPENMP package (Chun-Yeol You, Daegu Gyeongbuk Institute of Science and Technology) PR #5234 \r\n- add inertial spin dynamics, referred to as TSPIN, to the LAMMPS SPIN package (Zhengtao Huang, University of Hong Kong) PR #5157 \r\n- add chunk based compute for coarse graining granular fields (Joel Clemmer, SNL) PR #5092\r\n- add more /gapsys soft core pair styles to the FEP package (Evangelos Voyiatzis at National Technical University of Athens) PR #5162\r\n- revise Stillinger-Weber family pair styles to yield significant performance improvements (Yoel Sevi, Google DeepMind) PR #5275 \r\n- add some new features to enable more accurate and robust NEMD shearing simulations of dense liquids of rigid bodies (Steve Plimpton) PR #4577\r\n- add a `molindex` keyword to `fix gcmc`  to select a specific molecule from a molecule template (Russell Kajouri, University of Stuttgart) PR #5156\r\n- Use updated Pauli repulsion conventions of the current Tinker code for the HIPPO force field in the AMOEBA package (Paul Saxe, MolSSI and Virginia Tech) PR #5261\r\n- Fix polarization forces and virial with equal Ewald coefficients; also fix the induced dipole predictors (Paul Saxe, MolSSI and Virginia Tech) PR #5258)\r\n- add typelabel support to KOKKOS (Jichen Li, Uppsala University) PR #5205\r\n- Bug fix and cleanup for compute pace, a new per-atom style compute pace/atom, and unit tests for both (Anders Johansson, SNL) PR #5283 \r\n- add new presets for more aggressive optimization and documentation about the options and risks (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5302 \r\n- convert PDF documents for the SPH, MACHDYN, and PERI package to Howto documents (Axel Kohlmeyer, Temple U) PR #5263 \r\n- Many small bug fixes, minor code improvements and refactoring, and updates for coding style, build system, testing, documentation, and formatting (multiple authors): PR #5040, PR #5224, PR #5225, PR #5228, PR #5236, PR #5237, PR#5238, PR #5240, PR #5241, PR #5244, PR #5245, PR #5250, PR #5256, PR #5260, PR #5270, PR #5273, PR #5276, PR #5293, PR #5307, PR #5308, PR #5309, PR #5310, PR #5325\r\n\r\nFull git Changelog: https://github.com/lammps/lammps/compare/patch_30Sep2026...patch_17Nov2026\r\n\r\n## Backward compatibility notes:\r\n- The minimum CMake version was raised from 3.20 to 3.27 \r\n- The CUDA toolkit version 12.0 or later is required to compile the GPU package for CUDA\r\n- The ROCm/HIP compiler version 6.x or later is required to compile the GPU package with HIP (for AMD, Nvidia, or Intel GPUs)\r\n- The NVIDIA GPU architecture is now only the number without the 'sm_' prefix and semicolon separated list of multiple architecures is supported; default is now 'all-major'.\r\n- Any code accessing internal Modify class members (e.g. nfix or fix[] or ncompute and so on) needs to be rewritten to use available accessors, also atom->grow callbacks have a different API now.\r\n\r\n## Information on the files attached to this release:\r\n\r\n- **lammps-src-13Nov2026.tar.gz** - source code with translated manual in HTML and PDF format included\r\n- **lammps-linux-x86_64-13Nov2026.tar.gz** - Fully static LAMMPS binaries for *all* Linux machines with x86_64 CPUs\r\n- **Manual-13Nov2026.pdf** - LAMMPS manual as PDF\r\n- **lammps-gui-v3.1.3.pdf** - Manual for LAMMPS-GUI version v3.1.3 as PDF\r\n- The following packages contain LAMMPS 13Nov2026 and LAMMPS-GUI v3.1.3 pre-compiled in different packaging formats\r\n  +  **LAMMPS-Linux-x86_64-GUI-13Nov2026.tar.gz** - Binaries with required libraries included using wrapper scripts. Compatible with RHEL 9 or later and Ubuntu 22.04LTS or later and equivalent Linux distributions\r\n  + **LAMMPS-Linux-x86_64-GUI-13Nov2026.flatpak** - Linux binaries in flatpak bundle format and desktop integration\r\n  + **LAMMPS-macOS-multiarch-GUI-13Nov2026.dmg** - DMG installer for macOS version 12 (Monterey) or later. Includes support for Intel and Apple CPUs\r\n  + **LAMMPS-Win10-x64-GUI-13Nov2026.exe** - Installer package for 64-bit x86 Windows 10 or later.\r\n\r\nThe file `SHA256SUMS` contains the SHA-256 checksums and has been signed with GPG and its signature is in `SHA256SUMS.asc`. The corresponding public key to verify the signature is in https://github.com/akohlmey.gpg\r\n\r\nIf you are looking for a pre-compiled LAMMPS-GUI version that can load a custom compiled LAMMPS shared library (version 2 September 2026 or later) [please go to the LAMMPS-GUI release page](https://github.com/akohlmey/lammps-gui/releases)."
    }
  ]
